# Autonomy levels — {{ project_name }}

What the agent may do on its own, per task, and how a task earns more. The current level
of every task is in `.claude/autonomy.json`; the hooks in `.claude/hooks/` enforce it, so
this document explains the numbers rather than asking anyone to remember them.

## Levels

| Level | Meaning | What the agent does |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Propose only | Drafts the artefact and stops. A human executes. |
| 1 | Execute after explicit approval | Drafts, waits for an explicit yes in the session, then executes and reports with evidence. |
| 2 | Execute and report | Executes without asking, reports what it did with evidence, and the human reviews before anything leaves the repo. |
| 3 | Autonomous with review afterwards | Executes, commits or opens the PR, and the review happens on the result. |

