## Promotion

A task moves up one level when all of the following hold, and only then:

1. The skill or workflow that performs it has an eval suite with at least 3 cases, one
   of which is a refusal case.
2. Over the last **30 runs**, the graders and the human labels agree on **≥ 90 %** of
   runs, and the pass rate is **≥ 95 %**.
3. No gate violation (hook block, CI red caused by the agent) in the same window.
4. The QA engineer changes the number in `.claude/autonomy.json` in a PR that cites the
   eval report. The agent never edits that file (the `protect_paths` hook refuses).

Tasks capped by consequence (`case-approve`, `merge-pr`{% if has_comm_platform %}, `comm-post`{% endif %},
`execute-on-staging` at 2) stay capped whatever the numbers say.

## Demotion

Any single gate violation drops the task one level immediately, recorded in the same
file with the date and the run that caused it. It climbs back through the promotion
rule, not through time.

## Session override

`QI_AUTONOMY_OVERRIDE="execute-on-staging=2"` raises a level for one session, for the
QA engineer sitting next to the agent. It is never set in CI or in a script.

## TDD phases

`QI_PHASE=red` lets the agent edit only tests; `QI_PHASE=implement` freezes tests. Unset
means both are open. The `protect_paths` hook enforces it.

## Checking the hooks

```bash
python3 .claude/hooks/protect_paths.py --self-test
python3 .claude/hooks/guard_bash.py --self-test
python3 .claude/hooks/stop_gate.py --self-test
```
